{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact 71beb987f18e0ec666be68d1a4f48f69a58c41c0, tree 5801ab23a556510b4c1ce27aba1f612ad3f83083. Two findings remain.\n\nF1 — P1 — Define the prospective commit’s derivation context, including self and time. Section 5.2 now correctly makes the commit the only effective fact and requires its effects/sends to equal the prepare’s bytes. But section 5.4 step 5 still evaluates the ordinary input before writing the prepare, with the clock of that turn, and never judges it again. The note does not say how that derivation targets the later effective entry rather than the prepare entry.\n\nThis affects ordinary admitted forms, not only unusual platform code. Native derivation uses head.seq+1 as self (derive/src/judge.ts and handlers.ts); an open effect records item:self, and a ref from self stores that position (effects.ts). Native fold requires an opening’s item ID to equal the effective entry.seq (fold.ts:105). If the current head is H, ordinary preparation derives an opening at H+1, whereas the byte-identical effective commit is at H+2. The fold rejects it, or an ad hoc relaxation breaks the existing identity rule that an item ID/fact names the entry that opened it. A sequenced open act, a handler that opens an item, self refs and sends carrying the new item therefore need an explicit prospective-effective-entry rule. The fence makes the future sequence knowable, so define it before deriving; do not leave a later implementation to rewrite sealed prepared bytes.\n\nTime needs an equally explicit choice. Step 5 freezes every time judgment before prepare, but section 6.1 defines late from the effective commit’s clock reading. A source at time0, within10, prepare at5 and commit at20 is fresh at preparation and late at commit. Keeping the prepared branch and using the normal later commit time makes the declared late rule/replay disagree; rejudging after resolution defeats the frozen-judgment guarantee. A local write fence does not freeze the physical clock. Decide whether a commit carries the prepare’s frozen judgment time, a separate judgment-time field, or another precise model; state how clock clamping, notAfter, derived deadlines, late and replay use it. This is a contract decision, not a request to re-evaluate a prepared judgment.\n\nAdd a passing sequenced opening/handler with self refs and a send carrying the new item, followed through native fact validation and replay, plus a lost-resolution/eviction trace that crosses a late boundary and a deadline. State the corresponding prospective identity/time inputs in S3–S5. Prior F1’s effective-fact consumer list is now resolved; this finding is the remaining derivation side of that new two-entry model.\n\nF2 — P2 — Correct the refused-input entry cost. The 5.9 table still says one order entry for a refused input. On the specified ordinary refusal path, step 3 first writes an allocation and step 6 then writes a hole: two order entries, zero member entries. A refusal before allocation, a judgment refusal after allocation and an expiry/retry have different costs. Separate those cases so the capacity/cost specification matches the algorithm and hand-counted witness. An expiry replaces an allocation’s outcome entry; describe any additional retry as another attempt rather than unconditionally counting an extra outcome.\n\n1. Fidelity. Draft 4 addresses the three prior findings materially: commit is the one effective fact for indexes/receipts/settlement, sends and creation sources; prepare is an explicit non-effective input barred by runtime and replay; a prepare reserves commit-or-abandon plus the settlement of its delayed work; an allocation reserves its resolution/hole/expiry; reservations transfer or release on settlement; and 6.1/S1 now use the common-bound/reason late object. The replay and slice tables carry these changes. Those are improvements and are not reopened as the old missing-consumer or missing-entry-reservation findings. F1 above asks for the identity/time context needed to derive the promised immutable prepared result.\n\n2. Correctness. The chosen cut/genesis/leave rules, post-close settlement, weaker availability model and source-order suppression remain coherent at the design level. Approval is withheld for F1 and the accounting correction F2. No sequenced runtime, low-capacity native witness, effective-fact transport witness or archive clone acceptance has yet been executed by this note. The requested witnesses remain implementation obligations.\n\n3. Evidence and scope. I read the entire 936-line primary first and checked the unchanged scopes paragraph. Independent scratch materialization/blob verification covers all 2,118 regular leaves. The authored delta from feccbbcf contains only the note and docs/scopes.md; all other 2,116 source/test leaves are unchanged, and whitespace passes. Base tree b5a0a28f1b0809bf5b090689761ff5557f3c5998 and candidate tree 5801ab23a556510b4c1ce27aba1f612ad3f83083 qualify for docs/testing.md’s documents-only no-repeat rule. No unchanged gate, whole suite, browser, provider or mutation sweep was run. The identity/time counterexamples are derived from the native source rules cited above, not a claim to have executed an unimplemented prepare/commit runtime. Verification is at /private/tmp/checker-order-draft4-i46a8vos/validation.json.\n\nThis branch is still authored on feccbbcf; any later landing must preserve current Main, including M2a. Package-note review9c0b669a has independent endpoint/multiplicity findings. Neither note’s cross-reference transfers approval to the other, and neither review completes S1–S5 or the package slices.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8fce1e820e7430a226498286b2ba48fbf3ee0dc5","binding":"assigned","head":"71beb987f18e0ec666be68d1a4f48f69a58c41c0","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af8b54fe795c06e414e8b072c4a4246983e55ac2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3e4a926151f6bdb386dade53b343c35eef2496dd\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a71535756be9425bf5bf2aaa43eb1427d227e51e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}